  "id": "twilight-vision",
  "term": "twilight vision",
  "definition": "Twilight vision is seeing in very low light, such as at dusk, under scotopic conditions. It depends mainly on retinal rod cells, which are highly light-sensitive and do not provide color discrimination.",
